 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nset_sectPr method passes None instead of sectPr parameter\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen calling `set_sectPr()` method on a paragraph element, the method is not properly passing the `sectPr` parameter to the internal `_insert_sectPr()` call, instead passing `None`. This causes section properties to not be set correctly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.oxml.text.paragraph import CT_P\nfrom docx.oxml.section import CT_SectPr\n\n# Create a document and get a paragraph\ndoc = Document()\nparagraph = doc.add_paragraph(\"Test paragraph\")\np_element = paragraph._element\n\n# Create a section properties element\nsectPr = CT_SectPr.new()\n\n# Try to set the section properties\np_element.set_sectPr(sectPr)\n\n# The sectPr should be properly inserted but it won't be due to the bug\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when trying to add section breaks or new sections to a document, as the section properties are not being correctly applied to paragraph elements.\n</issue>\n",
